# =====================================================================
#  UserSelectsNode.ab
# =====================================================================
#  sentence   User Select Node
#  v4         selectNode(id)  — IMPLEMENTED
#             leftpanel_v4.html line 506.
#  triggers   click a row (line 427-432) · the row "more" button
#             (line 419) · right-click (line 439)
#
#  NOTE the term is `system select node` with resource NODE, even
#  when a File was clicked.  selection is the untyped view —
#  grammar R7 lets the actor change between sentence and step, and
#  the resource changes for the same reason: nothing about being
#  selected knows what kind of row it is.
#
#  this program HALTS instead of going to Redraw, and that is the
#  honest answer.  v4's selectNode() sets state.selected and calls
#  updateSelection() (lines 485-509), which walks existing rows
#  toggling the `.selected` class.  it repaints nothing, because
#  nothing structural changed — no counts, no tabs, no editor.
#  sending it to Redraw would claim four paints that never happen.
#  an unimplemented repaint is as wrong a trace as a missing one.

program UserSelectsNode

sentence  User Select Node
enter     node.select.requested

step system select node
  catch node.select.ok halt
